  "Id": 182,
  "Title": "ISMC Professor Chairs International Conference Session",
  "NewsSubTitle": "Dr Philip Wood chairs a session at the IMC in Leeds.",
  "NewsSummary": "Dr Philip Wood chaired a session on Change and Renewal in Non-Muslim Communal Outlooks in the Classical Islamic Period",
  "GlobalNews": false,
  "AlternateNewsTitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSubtitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSummary": null,
  "NewsContent": "<p>Dr Wood, an expert in the intersection of political and religious ideas in the late antique Middle East, chaired a session on Change and Renewal in Non-Muslim Communal Outlooks in the Classical Islamic Period on Thursday 9th July. Concentrating on aspects of adaptation, adjustment, and modification by <a href=\"https://imc.leeds.ac.uk/dbsql02/AQueryServlet?%2aid=30&amp;%2aformId=30&amp;%2acontext=IMC&amp;conference=2015&amp;sessionId=5618&amp;chosenPaperId=&amp;%2aservletURI=https://imc.leeds.ac.uk/dbsql02/AQueryServlet\">non-Muslim communities</a> in the context of life under Muslim rule, speakers looked at social and administrative change. More information about the session is available here.</p>",
